00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.940
the audience what Deep
Learning Indaba is about?

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.398
NYALLENG MOOROSI: Our line is
strengthening African machine

00:01:45.398 --> 00:01:47.740
learning, so it's always
good to start with that.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.020
But I think the Deep Learning
Indaba has become strengthening

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.840
African machine learning, but
I think when we started it,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.130
we did not know exactly
how much it would.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.990
And it has become a community
of sharing knowledge,

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.230
of sharing skill, of
celebrating one another,

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.750
and of course,
continual learning.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.320
So it almost feels
like it's going

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.289
to be our yearly
pilgrimage, where

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:13.130
from wherever we come from, we
go to wherever everybody is,

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.170
and we collaborate,
and we work together,

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.780
and we just, we catch
up and we celebrate

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.169
what we did with the last year.

00:02:19.169 --> 00:02:19.960
WILLIE BRINK: Yeah.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.710
And I think also what
is very important

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:27.350
for us is to equip students and
academics from all over Africa

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.870
to come together, to meet each
other, to network, but very

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:34.190
importantly also, to go back
to their own communities

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.960
and carry on this message of
strengthening machine learning,

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.810
and really just catching up
with the rest of the world.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.750
Africa has enormous
potential, and I

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.840
think it's a very exciting
time for all of us.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.480
MELANIE WARRICK: Agreed.

